WEBVTT

00:01.560 --> 00:04.480
From yesterday's me to today's me.

00:05.140 --> 00:08.270
"You will lose your memory every thirteen hours."

00:09.020 --> 00:12.280
"It's the result of a traffic accident that happened four years ago."

00:12.940 --> 00:15.910
"I'm sorry to tell you that you also lost your left eye."

00:16.610 --> 00:20.490
"Please accept what has happened is real."

00:21.790 --> 00:26.330
"Here, I will write down what you need to know for you to live on."

00:27.040 --> 00:32.300
"First, please, without fail, read this diary every morning."

00:32.840 --> 00:34.840
"This is your memory."

00:35.430 --> 00:37.930
"Everything of yours is here."

00:38.930 --> 00:42.680
"Second, please make sure to write in the diary."

00:43.220 --> 00:46.690
"What you did that day, the conversations you had, medical records, etc."

00:46.690 --> 00:49.400
"Please write them down as accurately as you can."

00:50.610 --> 00:53.440
Fly high, make it

00:53.440 --> 00:56.700
Get to the new world that I seek

00:56.910 --> 01:03.200
Someday with my little wings

01:03.370 --> 01:09.460
Don't look back to the sorrow I left behind

01:09.750 --> 01:15.670
Here's my real intention I hide

01:16.300 --> 01:22.430
I wish you were here, and so just right by my side

01:22.720 --> 01:28.810
Need to be strong enough to swallow my pride

01:29.020 --> 01:34.730
I have been looking for my own style

01:34.730 --> 01:42.200
Don't give it up, here comes the life

01:45.120 --> 01:47.870
Be alive, take it

01:47.870 --> 01:51.130
Promise to find, yes I will

01:51.420 --> 01:57.590
Shining wings filled with wishes

01:57.880 --> 02:00.680
Fly high, make it

02:00.680 --> 02:04.140
Get to the new world that I seek

02:04.180 --> 02:10.650
Someday, so I believe

02:25.700 --> 02:30.120
"Third, if possible, please avoid coming into contact with strangers."

02:30.920 --> 02:37.300
"Due to this handicap, you might have a hard time or might trouble the person you've met."

02:37.960 --> 02:39.880
"In case you meet someone,

02:39.880 --> 02:44.470
please write down that person's exact characteristics and information in the diary."

02:47.350 --> 02:48.560
At first,

02:48.980 --> 02:57.190
I wrote down that you're a small, older guy in a school uniform, who came to the station around three o'clock.

02:57.190 --> 02:58.280
Older?

03:00.360 --> 03:04.740
Because for me, time stopped four years ago.

03:05.240 --> 03:06.990
Ah, I see.

03:07.450 --> 03:10.250
If you wore plain clothes on holidays,

03:10.250 --> 03:14.420
or if I met you before three o'clock, I wouldn't recognize you.

03:15.170 --> 03:16.750
So that's how it was.

03:20.300 --> 03:22.300
That's as far as you can read.

03:22.800 --> 03:25.430
Ah, sorry. This is a diary after all.

03:25.430 --> 03:26.180
No.

03:26.640 --> 03:28.720
This is the real me.

03:31.310 --> 03:36.150
Thirteen hours. That's the number of hours you can remember.

03:36.480 --> 03:42.990
I remember from when I get up at seven o'clock in the morning until eight o'clock in the evening.

03:42.990 --> 03:48.580
But, after that, an hour of my memories disappears as each hour passes.

03:49.080 --> 03:54.750
At twelve o'clock midnight, my memories from before eleven o'clock in the morning will be gone.

03:56.040 --> 03:58.840
And then at seven o'clock the next morning,

03:58.840 --> 04:03.340
my memories before six o'clock,
the previous evening, will be gone.

04:04.840 --> 04:07.550
In that case, when you get up in the morning,

04:07.550 --> 04:09.390
you'll have forgotten all about your encounter with me...

04:09.890 --> 04:12.640
No, I will remember.

04:14.810 --> 04:19.650
I think back upon things that are important to me. Many, many times.

04:20.320 --> 04:25.570
If I manage to recall them, I'm able to remember them for the next thirteen hours.

04:28.700 --> 04:30.870
At nine o'clock in the evening, before I go to sleep,

04:30.870 --> 04:34.120
I read the diary and think back upon the things that are important to me.

04:34.120 --> 04:38.130
If I do that, I'm able to remember them even the next morning.

04:39.210 --> 04:41.670
The fact that I had fun with you,

04:41.670 --> 04:45.760
and the fact that I have a memory defect.

04:47.680 --> 04:50.350
I live a peaceful life right now.

04:50.640 --> 04:55.640
I don't go to school, and since I don't have anyone whom I can call a friend...

04:56.310 --> 04:58.150
I'm really doing nothing at all.

04:58.770 --> 05:03.280
If I space out at the station, then I won't have anything I need to remember.

05:04.690 --> 05:07.360
It's a worthless life, isn't it?

05:07.700 --> 05:11.490
If I let go of everything, life will be very easy.

05:13.290 --> 05:14.950
That's not true-

05:13.950 --> 05:16.290
I don't have anything.

05:16.750 --> 05:22.300
Therefore, if I can, my goal is to live a life without troubling others.

05:23.000 --> 05:25.760
However, that's difficult as well.

05:25.760 --> 05:28.970
As long as I'm alive, I <i>will trouble someone.</i>

05:29.300 --> 05:34.310
And then I'll heartlessly forget that I troubled them.

05:35.310 --> 05:36.350
Renji-san.

05:36.730 --> 05:39.850
I'm going to tell you a joke.

05:40.060 --> 05:42.190
Eh? A joke?

05:44.730 --> 05:45.740
I'm home.

05:46.240 --> 05:49.280
Welcome back. Dinner is ready.

05:51.280 --> 05:56.120
Come to think of it, Renji, you got the career interest survey, didn't you?

05:56.120 --> 05:57.540
How do you know?

05:57.830 --> 06:00.880
I heard the other mothers talking about it in cooking class.

06:01.460 --> 06:05.300
That's pretty early. You're still a first-year student.

06:05.670 --> 06:06.300
Yeah.

06:06.670 --> 06:08.470
What will you write down?

06:08.470 --> 06:09.510
I don't know.

06:09.720 --> 06:12.510
It's fine if you just write down what you want to be.

06:12.930 --> 06:15.770
If I could decide, I wouldn't be stressed over it.

06:17.430 --> 06:22.440
Oh yeah, there's something I'd like you to deliver to Kuze-san after this.

06:22.860 --> 06:24.610
Kuze-san is back?

06:24.940 --> 06:25.940
Yeah.

06:25.940 --> 06:30.240
The pot on the stove is his share. Bring it to him.

06:30.240 --> 06:31.530
Yeah.

06:34.700 --> 06:35.790
Kuze-san.

06:37.700 --> 06:39.710
Oh, if it isn't Renji.

06:40.250 --> 06:41.580
It's been a long time.

06:42.210 --> 06:46.750
You're as short as ever. Have you been eating properly?

06:46.750 --> 06:50.130
After three months, is that the first thing you've got to say?

06:50.130 --> 06:52.760
Oh, is that my usual share?

06:52.760 --> 06:55.010
Yes. My mom told you to enjoy.

06:55.680 --> 06:57.520
I accept it gratefully.

06:57.520 --> 06:59.560
I wonder what today's dish is.

06:59.560 --> 07:02.690
Erm, can I come in?

07:02.690 --> 07:04.520
There's something I want to talk to you about.

07:04.810 --> 07:09.240
Yeah, if you don't mind that there's a girl on my bed who's wearing nothing.

07:10.780 --> 07:12.280
Excuse me for interrupting you.

07:12.280 --> 07:15.200
It's okay. We don't mind.

07:15.200 --> 07:17.240
I do, so forget about it.

07:17.540 --> 07:18.830
Well, you're right.

07:19.750 --> 07:20.750
Worrying over something?

07:21.120 --> 07:24.040
No, it's not a big deal.

07:24.330 --> 07:25.590
That's all right then.

07:26.000 --> 07:29.010
I'll visit your place with a souvenir next time.

07:29.010 --> 07:33.090
After you're finished with the pot, please leave it in front of my house.

07:33.090 --> 07:34.340
Thank you for everything.

07:35.010 --> 07:37.220
Good night, Renji. Sweet dreams.

07:38.600 --> 07:40.600
Welcome back, Kuze-san.

07:42.940 --> 07:44.230
I'm leaving.

07:44.230 --> 07:45.770
Be careful.

07:46.610 --> 07:49.280
The same peaceful day as usual.

07:49.280 --> 07:53.700
I feel that way because I remember my usual life.

07:54.570 --> 07:57.330
I was happy to see Kuze-san yesterday.

07:57.330 --> 08:01.040
That's because I remember Kuze-san.

08:03.870 --> 08:04.870
But for Chihiro,

08:05.420 --> 08:10.130
both the day she lived and the people she met disappear from her memory after thirteen hours.

08:12.090 --> 08:17.350
I went to see Chihiro simply because I wanted to see her.

08:20.060 --> 08:26.190
But Chihiro has to be mentally prepared to meet a stranger like me.

08:27.060 --> 08:29.610
I bet she feels anxious and scared.

08:30.020 --> 08:31.110
Yet...

08:31.990 --> 08:32.820
See you tomorrow.

08:33.190 --> 08:35.320
Yes. See you tomorrow.

08:37.030 --> 08:41.740
Is it all right for me to go and see Chihiro with such an irresponsible attitude?

08:41.740 --> 08:45.120
If you want to stay by Chihiro's side, you have to be prepared.

08:45.460 --> 08:49.590
Am I just being half-hearted about Chihiro?

08:52.380 --> 08:53.840
She won't be there today.

09:01.180 --> 09:04.100
I'm going to tell you a joke.

09:04.560 --> 09:05.770
A joke?

09:07.440 --> 09:14.400
Every day I think about how I can disappear without troubling anyone.

09:16.070 --> 09:19.200
But I've given up on that idea.

09:19.200 --> 09:21.200
I'm not afraid of disappearing.

09:22.330 --> 09:25.370
The feeling of being afraid will simply disappear as well.

09:25.370 --> 09:26.040
It's just that...

09:26.330 --> 09:27.170
Just that?

09:27.790 --> 09:33.630
What I'm truly afraid of is not the disappearance of my own memory,

09:33.630 --> 09:37.130
but disappearing from the memories of everyone else.

09:38.340 --> 09:43.770
I see. Surprisingly, I'm quite a coward.

09:44.720 --> 09:46.350
A joke... eh?

09:46.350 --> 09:47.020
A joke... eh?

09:48.140 --> 09:51.770
Isn't there something I can do for Chihiro?

09:51.770 --> 09:56.440
Something that a knight can do to protect his princess.

09:56.440 --> 09:58.530
Something that will make her happy.

09:58.950 --> 10:00.490
I have a dream.

10:00.490 --> 10:01.620
A dream?

10:01.620 --> 10:03.830
I want to write stories.

10:03.830 --> 10:07.540
Even if it's just a single story,
I want to complete one as my current self.

10:25.310 --> 10:27.310
How come you're here?

10:27.640 --> 10:29.270
I'm the messenger.

10:29.690 --> 10:34.770
Chihiro caught a cold. "Since I couldn't come here today, I'm sorry", she said.

10:35.150 --> 10:36.400
Is she all right?

10:37.400 --> 10:38.820
It's just an ordinary cold.

10:39.400 --> 10:43.240
To be safe, she's forbidden to go out today.

10:43.240 --> 10:44.490
I... see.

10:44.490 --> 10:45.410
I... see.

10:45.950 --> 10:48.370
Why didn't you come yesterday?

10:49.790 --> 10:52.920
You two made a promise, right? "See you tomorrow."

10:53.630 --> 10:56.920
Chihiro was here till midnight.

10:59.550 --> 11:06.100
To make up for her memory loss, Chihiro makes sure that she keeps that kind of promise.

11:06.810 --> 11:14.770
To her, "see you tomorrow" is an important promise that connects the her of that day to the her of a different day.

11:15.940 --> 11:17.530
I guess she was happy.

11:17.980 --> 11:21.200
Even though I came to pick her up, she told me she had made a promise with you.

11:21.950 --> 11:23.200
How stubborn.

11:24.870 --> 11:30.620
Since Chihiro cannot confirm her own existence, she listens to everything people tell her.

11:31.120 --> 11:34.790
It seems she still has some human qualities left in her.

11:35.880 --> 11:37.130
I... didn't even realize that.

11:37.130 --> 11:39.010
I... didn't even realize that.

11:39.800 --> 11:41.590
You're not the one to blame.

11:42.090 --> 11:48.560
Chihiro's inflexibility about her common sense just means I'm not qualified to be her guardian.

11:51.140 --> 11:51.980
Yeah.

11:52.640 --> 11:53.690
That's all.

12:06.030 --> 12:06.870
Mail

12:06.030 --> 12:06.870
Oomura

12:08.370 --> 12:09.910
Hello, Hirono speaking.

12:11.120 --> 12:13.710
Ah, I just have to write five more pages.

12:14.500 --> 12:15.790
Assistant?

12:15.790 --> 12:17.040
I don't need one.

12:17.040 --> 12:19.420
I've never lost a manuscript before, right?

12:20.130 --> 12:21.630
I'm in the middle of work...

12:22.470 --> 12:23.970
Ah, I understand.

12:24.300 --> 12:25.260
Goodbye.

12:30.390 --> 12:30.890
Incoming Mail

12:30.390 --> 12:30.890
Regarding my practice tomorrow

12:30.390 --> 12:30.890
Shindou Kei

12:30.890 --> 12:35.390
Incoming Mail

12:30.890 --> 12:35.390
Shindou Kei

12:30.890 --> 12:35.390
Regarding my practice tomorrow

12:32.060 --> 12:35.390
Tomorrow, I have morning practice so I won't be there to wake you up.

12:35.390 --> 12:38.650
Shindou Kei

12:35.390 --> 12:38.650
Regarding my practice tomorrow

12:35.900 --> 12:38.650
Please get up on time and go to school by yourself...

12:38.650 --> 12:38.900
Regarding my practice tomorrow

12:39.020 --> 12:41.400
If you skip school, I'll kill you.

12:41.860 --> 12:44.570
You'll get in trouble someday, because you say things like that.

12:46.360 --> 12:52.660
Postscript !

12:46.700 --> 12:49.950
PS: Chihiro is feverish.

12:49.950 --> 12:52.660
Onii-chan, don't overwork and get a cold too.

12:55.500 --> 12:56.420
Well then.

12:57.170 --> 13:00.250
Skip school and die or don't skip and die.

13:00.590 --> 13:02.800
In that case, there's only one thing to do.

13:10.640 --> 13:12.770
Ah, Onii-chan.

13:13.220 --> 13:16.190
Yo. Practicing by yourself this morning?

13:16.190 --> 13:19.520
Nah. Everyone is too slow, so I left them behind.

13:19.860 --> 13:21.230
Let me have a sip.

13:22.150 --> 13:25.110
Aside from that, what's wrong? You're up so early.

13:25.360 --> 13:27.990
I finished the script through sheer willpower.

13:27.990 --> 13:30.370
I just brought it to the editing department.

13:30.780 --> 13:34.500
If I fell asleep, I wouldn't be able to wake up, so I thought I'd head straight to school.

13:34.910 --> 13:37.290
What kind of wind is blowing?

13:37.290 --> 13:39.040
Is it going to rain too?

13:39.750 --> 13:42.250
I can't guarantee I'll be awake during class though.

13:42.550 --> 13:44.460
Then it's meaningless!

13:45.920 --> 13:47.340
You drank all of it...

13:47.510 --> 13:50.340
Well, I commend you for your solo efforts.

13:50.720 --> 13:53.350
Good work, Onii-chan.

13:55.060 --> 13:56.640
What was that about?

13:59.690 --> 14:00.860
Hey, Hirono.

14:00.860 --> 14:02.020
Still alive?

14:02.230 --> 14:03.860
You can tell by looking, right?

14:03.860 --> 14:05.150
I'm dead.

14:05.400 --> 14:09.570
You always look wasted at the end of the month...

14:09.950 --> 14:11.450
Is it <i>that day again?</i>

14:11.950 --> 14:13.530
Yeah, it's <i>that day again.</i>

14:13.830 --> 14:15.200
I see...

14:15.200 --> 14:16.700
It's hard, isn't it?

14:17.410 --> 14:19.460
I think I'll take a nap.

14:19.750 --> 14:21.670
Make sure you don't catch a cold.

14:29.300 --> 14:30.430
Guess who.

14:32.140 --> 14:34.390
Now, who am I?

14:40.560 --> 14:41.770
Hey you...

14:41.770 --> 14:45.440
Don't be mad. It's just a cute prank that's done all the time, right?

14:45.440 --> 14:47.610
Normally you only cover the eyes!

14:48.400 --> 14:50.400
Normal is no fun.

14:50.400 --> 14:52.950
You can't kill me for a reason like that!

14:53.370 --> 14:56.450
But I'm glad you're here.

14:57.580 --> 14:58.450
Why?

14:58.790 --> 15:01.460
Because, if you weren't here...

15:02.040 --> 15:05.630
The lock to such a wonderful hiding place couldn't be opened.

15:06.000 --> 15:07.590
Ah, I see.

15:07.590 --> 15:10.470
Hey, will you give that to me?

15:10.470 --> 15:11.340
No.

15:11.970 --> 15:15.970
It's an important souvenir my elder sister gave me as congratulations for being admitted to this school.

15:15.970 --> 15:18.640
Even a duplicate key is fine, then.

15:18.640 --> 15:22.270
There's no way I'm gonna share my precious space, where I can be alone.

15:24.860 --> 15:28.280
By the way, Hirono-kun. What about your job today?

15:28.280 --> 15:34.410
If you don't finish your script soon, will your editor beat you up?

15:34.410 --> 15:37.410
I wouldn't come to school under such circumstances.

15:37.410 --> 15:40.040
Really? Let's go, then.

15:40.410 --> 15:42.870
W-Wait a second. Where are we going?

15:43.370 --> 15:44.080
Somewhere that's not h-e-r-e.

15:44.080 --> 15:44.920
Somewhere that's not h-e-r-e.

15:44.920 --> 15:45.750
Somewhere that's not h-e-r-e.

15:45.750 --> 15:46.590
Somewhere that's not h-e-r-e.

15:46.590 --> 15:48.000
Somewhere that's not h-e-r-e.

15:53.300 --> 15:55.850
Somehow, it looks ordinary.

15:55.850 --> 15:57.890
What do you mean by "ordinary"?

15:58.600 --> 16:00.680
It's like it came out of a textbook.

16:00.680 --> 16:02.770
This kind of film is commonplace.

16:03.390 --> 16:05.980
We <i>made it to look ordinary.</i>

16:05.980 --> 16:09.900
It looks too much like Impressionism if we combine your shots together.

16:10.320 --> 16:12.280
What's wrong with that?

16:12.700 --> 16:17.580
Works that are too individualistic won't be considered for the special prize.

16:17.580 --> 16:22.000
If you plan to go after a high-ranking prize, a solid production will work better.

16:24.960 --> 16:26.540
Kyosuke...

16:26.960 --> 16:31.170
As I thought, even simply taking a walk in Otawa is fun.

16:31.170 --> 16:33.760
I've been living here forever, so I'm tired of seeing it.

16:34.010 --> 16:39.100
There might be a difference in the scenery you usually see when two people walk together.

16:39.100 --> 16:41.140
Not at all.

16:41.140 --> 16:46.190
This Otawa town had ordinary Japanese scenery before as well.

16:46.190 --> 16:48.860
It was all wiped out by the earthquake.

16:48.860 --> 16:52.900
It was also burned to ashes during the war. What an unlucky town.

16:53.360 --> 16:54.200
Maybe that's why...

16:55.030 --> 16:58.700
They built a town that was completely different from before.

17:02.830 --> 17:06.960
You don't need to hold back. I have money with me.

17:06.960 --> 17:09.750
I stayed up all night, so I can't eat that much.

17:11.500 --> 17:13.260
The weather is nice.

17:13.630 --> 17:17.340
There's no way I'd feel like attending class on a day like this.

17:17.340 --> 17:20.970
You skip school regardless of the weather, don't you?

17:20.970 --> 17:21.930
Yeah.

17:22.430 --> 17:24.270
Do you hate school?

17:24.270 --> 17:25.480
Nah.

17:25.480 --> 17:26.770
Why, then?

17:27.900 --> 17:30.770
The town is way more interesting than lessons.

17:31.150 --> 17:32.110
Huh?

17:32.110 --> 17:35.950
I don't hate school. I just hate being bored.

17:36.530 --> 17:38.820
In any case, isn't it better to choose the interesting one?

17:39.280 --> 17:43.540
Even though I shouldn't be the one to say so, it's bad not to go to school.

17:43.540 --> 17:48.040
If the world was restrained to common sense, life wouldn't be fun.

17:48.580 --> 17:52.710
You should also do things that you think you'd enjoy.

17:54.300 --> 17:55.800
Hiro-senpai!

17:56.050 --> 17:57.170
Hayama.

17:58.180 --> 18:01.600
Hiro-senpai, what are you doing at a place like this?

18:01.600 --> 18:03.680
What about you?

18:04.180 --> 18:06.100
I'm shopping.

18:06.100 --> 18:09.190
For my supply of shoujo manga.

18:09.190 --> 18:11.690
You really like manga, eh.

18:12.020 --> 18:14.440
Hirono-kun, who's she?

18:14.440 --> 18:18.490
Ah. She's my kouhai, Hayama Mizuki.

18:14.440 --> 18:18.490
A "kouhai" is a junior at school or work.

18:18.490 --> 18:19.700
Nice to meet you.

18:19.700 --> 18:22.120
She's my classmate, Miyamura.

18:22.120 --> 18:24.290
Miyamura... erm...

18:24.290 --> 18:25.540
What?!

18:26.870 --> 18:28.210
Hirono-kun.

18:28.210 --> 18:32.960
I order you to call me "Miyako" from this very moment on.

18:33.210 --> 18:34.800
What's that?

18:34.800 --> 18:41.010
My heart is thoroughly scarred because you forgot my name so quickly.

18:41.010 --> 18:44.050
I have no idea what I should do anymore.

18:44.470 --> 18:46.060
Say, Hayama.

18:46.060 --> 18:48.640
Do you think this is a threat?

18:48.640 --> 18:50.850
It's your fault.

18:50.850 --> 18:55.230
Besides, it's weird to call your girlfriend by her last name.

18:55.230 --> 18:58.240
Hiro-senpai is such a shy guy.

18:58.240 --> 18:59.570
She's not my girlfriend!

18:59.570 --> 19:01.780
E-Eh? Really?

19:01.780 --> 19:08.790
I thought that if you got a girlfriend, the available Kei-senpai would be mine.

19:08.790 --> 19:12.120
How come even Kei is now my girlfriend?

19:13.710 --> 19:15.460
Where's Miyamura?

19:15.460 --> 19:18.130
You got dumped.

19:18.130 --> 19:20.920
As I said, she's not my girlfriend!

19:22.720 --> 19:23.840
Kyosuke.

19:24.300 --> 19:27.510
I know how you feel, but try to understand.

19:27.510 --> 19:31.350
Everyone worked hard to win at this Cinema Festival.

19:31.350 --> 19:33.150
You guys always talk about that.

19:34.270 --> 19:36.730
The only thing you care about is the evaluation.

19:36.730 --> 19:39.940
You should stick to what you want to do.

19:40.530 --> 19:42.110
How about you?

19:42.110 --> 19:44.820
Are you sticking to what you want to do?

19:44.820 --> 19:45.700
No idea.

19:45.700 --> 19:46.950
"No idea"...

19:47.830 --> 19:50.620
Somehow, I'm bored lately.

19:50.620 --> 19:52.290
Peeking through the finder.

19:52.540 --> 19:53.830
What does that mean?

19:54.330 --> 19:57.840
I can't see what I want to do.

19:59.170 --> 20:00.460
Say, Kyosuke.

20:01.220 --> 20:01.970
What?

20:02.930 --> 20:05.050
Let's break up.

20:06.640 --> 20:11.230
Somehow I don't understand you anymore.

20:12.940 --> 20:14.690
You're right.

20:15.270 --> 20:18.480
Can you fill out the notice that I'm leaving the club, President?

20:19.860 --> 20:21.280
Kyosuke...

20:23.240 --> 20:25.860
The site of the earthquake, eh?

20:25.860 --> 20:27.240
It's still here.

20:30.990 --> 20:33.870
You can't stay here.

20:34.620 --> 20:40.630
There's no need to look back at the wreckage of a past that's already over.

20:41.300 --> 20:44.220
I only look forward all the time.

20:44.220 --> 20:48.640
Oh? Aren't you unable to see what you want to do?

20:48.640 --> 20:50.390
For now.

20:50.390 --> 20:54.520
But I decided what I wanted to do a long time ago.

20:54.810 --> 20:55.520
I...

20:56.100 --> 20:58.020
I take the shots I want to take.

20:58.730 --> 21:00.320
What's that?

21:01.020 --> 21:02.820
What I want to take is...

21:03.900 --> 21:04.900
A dream.

21:11.490 --> 21:16.290
The cold is nothing serious, but Himura-san won't let me go outside.

21:16.670 --> 21:18.790
Even though I want to go see Renji-kun.

21:19.330 --> 21:22.630
You have to listen to what Himura-san tells you.

21:22.630 --> 21:25.300
If you get worse, it'll be bad.

21:26.800 --> 21:28.640
INBOX

21:26.800 --> 21:28.640
Hayama Mizuki

21:26.800 --> 21:28.640
Shindou Chihiro

21:26.800 --> 21:28.640
Hayama Mizuki

21:26.800 --> 21:28.640
Hirono Hiro

21:27.630 --> 21:28.640
Mizuki?

21:34.890 --> 21:36.980
Hirono-kun, you idiot.

21:40.980 --> 21:42.440
Hey, Onii-chan.

21:42.440 --> 21:46.700
Don't yawn while watching someone practicing. It's rude.

21:46.700 --> 21:49.700
I'm on a different timetable than you.

21:49.700 --> 21:52.950
Humans should sleep at night and wake up in the morning, right?

21:52.950 --> 21:56.460
Manga artists are creatures who really live outside the confines of human nature.

21:56.710 --> 21:58.960
It doesn't matter.

21:58.960 --> 22:01.750
What do you want to talk to me about this early in the morning?

22:02.420 --> 22:04.960
You skipped school yesterday, didn't you?

22:06.470 --> 22:11.390
Y-Yeah. My body couldn't stand it after staying up all night.

22:11.390 --> 22:13.310
I went home to sleep in the afternoon.

22:13.310 --> 22:14.140
You liar.

22:15.470 --> 22:17.100
I know.

22:17.100 --> 22:19.730
You were with Miyamura-senpai, right?

22:21.310 --> 22:24.440
I heard from Mizuki. You ran into her, didn't you?

22:24.820 --> 22:26.570
You know Miyamura?

22:27.150 --> 22:29.110
She's famous.

22:29.110 --> 22:32.700
You're about the only one who doesn't know, since you don't come to school.

22:32.700 --> 22:34.200
Really?

22:34.830 --> 22:39.160
Because she's pretty, the guys always talk about her.

22:39.160 --> 22:40.920
She's a habitual school-skipper,

22:40.920 --> 22:45.840
and even when she attends class once in a while, she completely ignores what the teacher says.

22:45.840 --> 22:48.260
When she's called on, she doesn't answer.

22:49.800 --> 22:53.350
Your attendance record is already dangerously bad.

22:53.350 --> 22:57.390
She didn't know the circumstances,
yet she just took you out as she liked.

22:57.390 --> 22:59.390
What an annoying girl.

22:59.730 --> 23:04.060
Stop bad-mouthing someone you don't really know!

23:04.400 --> 23:08.650
Do you know Miyamura-senpai well, then?

23:08.900 --> 23:10.150
I don't.

23:10.150 --> 23:12.700
T-The first time we met was Christmas.

23:12.700 --> 23:14.660
It hasn't been a month yet.

23:14.660 --> 23:16.410
Christmas...?

23:16.700 --> 23:18.250
Is that true?

23:20.160 --> 23:26.210
Onii-chan, you broke your promise to me because you met Miyamura-senpai?

23:49.110 --> 23:55.870
Since you're by my side when I turn around,

23:56.950 --> 24:02.460
I could not be honest

24:02.580 --> 24:04.920
Because someday

24:05.290 --> 24:18.220
I want to convey the feelings of my wavering self

24:18.680 --> 24:28.020
The unchanging time, your voice,

24:28.110 --> 24:35.610
Your kindness is suffocating

24:35.610 --> 24:44.040
I'm hiding the confusion in my uneasy eyes

24:44.080 --> 24:50.710
It hurts to smile

24:58.180 --> 25:02.180
I entrust the feelings that I want to convey in the story.

25:02.270 --> 25:07.440
Next episode, ef - a tale of memories: honesty.

25:07.520 --> 25:10.440
Do you have memories you don't want to forget?
